title: "AI_DNA_ANALYZER: frozen-constant statistical SNP variant calling with confidence routing"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Mark
    family-names: Kostogryzov
repository-code: "https://github.com/Kramkost/AI_DNA_ANALYZER"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.22978775
version: 2.0.0
date-released: "2026-09-26"
license: GPL-3.0-only
keywords:
  - bioinformatics
  - genomics
  - variant calling
  - SNP
  - Poisson-binomial
  - confidence routing
  - Genome in a Bottle
  - hap.py
  - htslib
  - statistical genetics
abstract: >-
  A cheap binomial screen calls every locus; a fixed router sends only the
  loci near its decision boundary to a slower per-read Poisson-binomial
  model. The project measures, with frozen thresholds and a pre-registered
  verdict rule, whether that saves compute without changing the SNP calls
  it makes, validated against GIAB benchmark samples.
